WEBVTT

00:15.590 --> 00:18.600
You're awfully cheery about a 
little stack of papers, Will.

00:19.620 --> 00:20.910
You could tell?

00:20.910 --> 00:21.840
Yeah.

00:21.840 --> 00:23.910
You were grinning and stroking that paper

00:23.910 --> 00:26.160
the way someone would stroke a woman's skin.

00:27.870 --> 00:30.640
Is that the stuff those 
craftsmen presented to you?

00:30.640 --> 00:33.630
They said these were the best of 
all the trial sheets they made.

00:35.360 --> 00:37.380
You really are happy, aren't you?

00:41.820 --> 00:42.930
Well, these...

00:43.640 --> 00:45.770
are the future of this town, after all.

00:51.940 --> 00:54.010
Man, it's cold.

00:54.010 --> 00:55.860
It's almost the winter solstice.

00:58.590 --> 01:00.410
It's a lot livelier these days.

01:00.410 --> 01:01.190
Yeah.

01:02.120 --> 01:04.560
<i>Two years ago, I left the City of the Dead</i>

01:04.560 --> 01:06.740
<i>and followed the river north,</i>

01:06.740 --> 01:09.660
<i>until I found a deserted, half-sunken city.</i>

01:10.240 --> 01:13.300
<i>Now, two years after rebuilding began,</i>

01:13.300 --> 01:18.250
<i>people are calling this place 
Torch Port, the port of light.</i>

01:18.930 --> 01:23.050
Will, what did you mean when you said 
that paper was this town's future?

01:23.370 --> 01:26.970
If all we do is cut down all the lumber 
around here and sell it to Whitesails,

01:26.970 --> 01:29.160
the city will eventually run 
out of trees and die out.

01:29.680 --> 01:32.950
So we need to diversify trade in this town.

01:33.400 --> 01:34.930
We'll be better off for it in ten years.

01:34.930 --> 01:37.220
And that's what that paper is?

01:37.220 --> 01:39.670
It's the first step, 
and one worth celebrating.

01:39.670 --> 01:40.960
Hmm...

01:40.960 --> 01:44.230
You know, you think like an elf sometimes.

01:45.000 --> 01:47.830
You're just the type that 
lives in the moment.

01:47.830 --> 01:51.940
We're basically at the ends of 
the earth. I could die tomorrow.

01:52.720 --> 01:54.840
So I want to feel satisfied today.

01:55.190 --> 02:00.460
I'm sure most people living here 
feel that way, including me.

02:01.330 --> 02:03.620
And I want to change that.

02:07.520 --> 02:11.720
Well, maybe that's why the 
goddess of light chose you.

02:11.720 --> 02:12.250
Huh?

02:12.250 --> 02:15.600
You're right in the middle of the front 
line, where you could die at any time,

02:15.600 --> 02:19.780
talking about planting the seeds 
that'll benefit us in ten years.

02:23.200 --> 02:24.510
By the way...

02:24.880 --> 02:27.500
The brother of the crown prince 
of Whitesails invited us

02:27.500 --> 02:30.490
to the new year's ceremony. Gonna go?

02:30.490 --> 02:33.430
Oh... That's right.

02:41.260 --> 02:46.850
The Faraway Paladin

02:43.050 --> 02:46.850
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

04:36.500 --> 04:38.750
Wow! How pretty!

04:39.500 --> 04:42.500
Well? Did you enjoy the 
winter solstice festival?

04:42.500 --> 04:45.890
Yeah, it was fun. I'm worn out, though.

04:45.890 --> 04:49.490
Going around greeting all the 
important people with a smile

04:49.490 --> 04:52.020
isn't as easy as it looks, huh?

04:52.330 --> 04:54.820
But thanks to Menel putting 
my outfit together

04:54.820 --> 04:57.390
and all the help I got from Bishop Bagley,

04:57.390 --> 04:59.270
I managed to pull it off.

04:59.270 --> 05:02.340
I wanted to see Menel in formal clothes!

05:02.340 --> 05:04.250
Where is Menel, anyway?

05:04.610 --> 05:06.480
I invited him, but he said,

05:06.480 --> 05:10.320
"Shut up! At least let me sleep 
in on the day of the event!"

05:11.360 --> 05:13.680
What about you? Did you make a profit?

05:13.680 --> 05:14.700
Of course!

05:14.700 --> 05:18.050
This is the most profitable 
time of year for a troubadour!

05:25.640 --> 05:26.790
What is it?

05:27.250 --> 05:30.220
I was just thinking, 
this town really is beautiful.

05:30.220 --> 05:33.060
The forests around the 
Beast Woods are still very poor.

05:33.740 --> 05:36.010
We have to work a lot harder.

05:38.520 --> 05:39.410
Will.

05:47.450 --> 05:48.350
Bop!

05:49.600 --> 05:51.550
You're worrying too much.

05:52.090 --> 05:53.170
Bee...

05:53.170 --> 05:55.790
You do have a tendency to do that.

05:59.340 --> 06:01.040
I made a promise...

06:01.950 --> 06:04.910
that I'd be as the goddess's 
sword to banish evil,

06:04.910 --> 06:08.420
and be as her hand to save the suffering.

06:11.280 --> 06:13.600
It's wonderful of you to have 
such benevolent intentions,

06:13.600 --> 06:15.490
and it's very noble of you,

06:15.490 --> 06:18.810
but if that's the case, you should be 
trying to please the goddess more!

06:19.170 --> 06:20.440
Please her?

06:20.440 --> 06:22.280
Just think about it!

06:22.280 --> 06:24.970
What if a villager brought you 
food to show his gratitude,

06:24.970 --> 06:28.580
but he himself was scrawny 
and unsteady on his feet?

06:28.580 --> 06:30.810
I'd tell him to eat it himself...

06:32.570 --> 06:35.320
Don't you think the goddess 
would feel the same?

06:36.820 --> 06:37.940
Yeah.

06:39.190 --> 06:40.730
Thanks, Bee.

06:40.730 --> 06:43.970
To thank you, I'll take you 
wherever you want to go.

06:44.370 --> 06:47.110
My, what an enthusiastic proposition!

06:47.110 --> 06:48.180
I accept!

06:52.360 --> 06:54.270
Bee, were you serious?

06:54.270 --> 06:57.640
Absolutely serious! 
There's something I want to see.

06:57.640 --> 07:03.700
But it's not the kind of place a lowly 
troubadour can get into just by asking nicely.

07:03.700 --> 07:05.860
You could sneak in, though, right?

07:05.860 --> 07:09.230
'Cause on top of being a warrior 
priest, you're a great sorcerer!

07:11.600 --> 07:15.580
<i>A school attended by sorcerers 
studying the Words of Creation,</i>

07:15.580 --> 07:17.840
<i>located in the woods in a forbidden land...</i>

07:17.840 --> 07:19.170
<i>The Academy.</i>

07:19.170 --> 07:20.910
Well, then, let's go!

07:20.910 --> 07:21.780
Wait.

07:23.890 --> 07:25.130
I think...

07:25.660 --> 07:28.220
this is Maze Alley magic.

07:28.220 --> 07:30.140
And several Signs...

07:30.350 --> 07:31.120
"Warning."

07:31.430 --> 07:32.140
"Paralysis."

07:32.140 --> 07:33.130
"Sleep."

07:33.130 --> 07:34.190
"Blind."

07:34.910 --> 07:36.930
Yeah, we can't go in.

07:36.930 --> 07:38.180
What?!

07:38.180 --> 07:40.380
Shouldn't you be able to go in?!

07:40.380 --> 07:42.970
With, you know, brute strength?!

07:42.970 --> 07:45.030
If we tried to force our way in,

07:45.030 --> 07:46.930
it'd be raining blood.

07:46.930 --> 07:48.530
And that's not a metaphor.

07:48.530 --> 07:49.590
Huh?!

07:49.590 --> 07:51.810
It's set up to prevent anyone 
from sneaking in uninvited.

07:52.880 --> 07:54.440
Oh...

07:57.230 --> 08:00.370
Well, if even you can't get it, 
I guess that's that!

08:00.370 --> 08:01.960
Let's head back to town and eat at a—

08:01.960 --> 08:03.710
We can't <i>sneak</i> in, but...

08:04.240 --> 08:05.250
Will?

08:07.340 --> 08:09.380
Let's just go up to the front door.

08:10.830 --> 08:13.200
That's a good idea!

08:21.640 --> 08:23.400
Er... huh?

08:23.690 --> 08:27.020
Which way did we get here from?

08:27.020 --> 08:30.660
Wait, what? I know in my head 
where we came from, but...

08:30.940 --> 08:33.930
It's okay. Just keep holding on to my hand.

08:45.540 --> 08:47.800
Well, this is just mean.

08:47.800 --> 08:50.650
Wh-Which is the wrong path?

08:52.420 --> 08:55.010
Ne Fronti Crede.

08:52.420 --> 08:55.010
Do Not Believe the Pretense

08:59.890 --> 09:00.850
Wha...

09:00.850 --> 09:02.260
This is the right one.

09:06.390 --> 09:09.890
"Either learn... or leave."

09:09.890 --> 09:12.890
If you will not learn, you must leave?

09:14.050 --> 09:15.010
Will...

09:15.550 --> 09:17.070
Don't push this, okay?

09:17.070 --> 09:20.300
Even the Wandering Sage in his youth

09:20.300 --> 09:23.080
couldn't pass through this route on his own.

09:23.080 --> 09:24.100
What?

09:24.100 --> 09:25.290
<i>Gus couldn't?</i>

09:25.570 --> 09:27.380
He was a child prodigy,

09:27.380 --> 09:32.210
yet he still couldn't visit the 
Academy without his master's help.

09:32.210 --> 09:34.720
That's how he learned just 
how immature he still was.

09:36.540 --> 09:38.210
<i>I see.</i>

09:38.210 --> 09:41.680
<i>So even Gus couldn't get through 
here when he was young.</i>

09:44.880 --> 09:46.950
What is this? A curse?

09:47.520 --> 09:50.500
Looking at it makes me feel really uneasy.

09:50.500 --> 09:54.640
Hmm... I can't really 
sense any mana at work...

09:54.640 --> 09:56.940
D-Doesn't that make it all 
the more suspicious?

09:56.940 --> 10:01.510
Setting a little trap in something 
obviously suspicious is classic!

10:03.240 --> 10:07.450
You're right. There's a Sign carved into 
it that makes one just a little uneasy.

10:07.450 --> 10:09.900
Boy, talk about twisted!

10:09.900 --> 10:12.330
I could write a song about this alone!

10:20.090 --> 10:21.230
Oh?

10:22.770 --> 10:24.970
What's this? Visitors?

10:24.970 --> 10:27.220
It's a pleasure to meet you.

10:27.220 --> 10:30.570
My name is William G. Maryblood.

10:30.570 --> 10:33.740
I'm Bee. Robina Goodfellow.

10:33.740 --> 10:38.320
Would you kindly tell 
us your name, good sir?

10:39.810 --> 10:44.490
I'm just an old man who's built 
up nothing but a lot of years.

10:44.490 --> 10:47.090
I'm the Academy's groundskeeper.

10:47.090 --> 10:51.000
My name is not worthy 
of giving to a paladin.

10:51.290 --> 10:53.810
More importantly, you must be cold.

10:53.810 --> 10:56.740
Why don't you rest here for a bit?

10:56.740 --> 10:58.250
Thank you very much.

10:59.520 --> 11:01.770
Tell us, kind groundskeeper.

11:01.770 --> 11:04.900
Is the Academy still far from here?

11:05.700 --> 11:10.060
For what purpose might you be 
visiting the Academy, young lady?

11:10.060 --> 11:14.520
You do not appear to be a new student.

11:14.520 --> 11:16.350
There's something I want to see!

11:16.350 --> 11:23.730
Oh? But the Academy has a rule 
that only sorcerers may enter.

11:24.300 --> 11:28.950
We were hoping to ask them if we might 
be allowed in for just a brief look.

11:28.950 --> 11:32.860
Well, I do hope you succeed 
in earning permission.

11:33.590 --> 11:37.580
Now, toast and eat these. 
They'll warm you up.

11:37.580 --> 11:39.670
Wow! Thank you!

11:39.670 --> 11:41.310
We gratefully accept.

11:57.980 --> 11:59.520
This is so good!

11:59.840 --> 12:02.350
It's cheese made from goat milk, isn't it?

12:02.350 --> 12:03.960
That's absolutely right.

12:03.960 --> 12:05.530
It really is good!

12:05.990 --> 12:11.360
Incidentally, I hear the Faraway Paladin 
has knowledge of magic.

12:11.360 --> 12:14.640
Yes, I have learned a bit.

12:14.640 --> 12:19.660
As the Academy's groundskeeper, 
I witness magic occasionally,

12:19.660 --> 12:25.750
but I am most interested in seeing 
what sort of magic you have.

12:26.300 --> 12:29.380
<i>I bet I'm being tested.</i>

12:29.870 --> 12:33.180
I'm unable to use my magic for mere sport.

12:33.960 --> 12:35.310
Please understand.

12:35.310 --> 12:38.310
Even if I beg to see it?

12:38.310 --> 12:39.830
Please understand.

12:39.830 --> 12:42.570
Has that always been your stance?

12:42.570 --> 12:43.760
Yes.

12:43.760 --> 12:45.410
It's what my master taught me,

12:45.410 --> 12:47.950
and I want to uphold it to 
the best of my ability.

12:48.800 --> 12:52.820
Hmm... In that case, 
might I ask a favor of you?

12:52.820 --> 12:54.210
Of course.

12:54.210 --> 12:57.760
Last night's snow has left 
all the trees quite damp,

12:57.760 --> 13:00.700
and my fire continues to smolder today.

13:00.700 --> 13:03.680
This is all quite tough on my old bones.

13:03.680 --> 13:06.720
I would like to have some dry firewood.

13:06.720 --> 13:09.980
Could you prepare some for me?

13:13.810 --> 13:18.400
<i>This problem would've been solved 
if I uttered the Words of Drying.</i>

13:19.870 --> 13:20.970
<i>But...</i>

13:24.350 --> 13:27.360
<i>You can dry damp wood over a fire.</i>

13:27.360 --> 13:30.030
<i>It's such common knowledge.</i>

13:32.870 --> 13:36.870
I do appreciate this. It's so nice and warm.

13:36.870 --> 13:41.010
Now, I have a question for the two of you.

13:41.010 --> 13:44.880
If great magic were to exist in this world,

13:44.880 --> 13:48.130
what do you think it would be like?

13:50.100 --> 13:53.470
Maybe it'd be magic that would 
bring people happiness?

13:53.470 --> 13:54.660
Oh?

13:55.270 --> 13:58.320
Whether it's the simplest Words 
used to create a smokescreen

13:58.320 --> 14:01.820
or a highly elaborate, artistic Sign...

14:01.820 --> 14:05.440
If it was woven with a 
prayer to bring happiness,

14:05.440 --> 14:08.040
I think it's plenty great.

14:08.470 --> 14:11.060
What an intriguing opinion.

14:11.060 --> 14:14.320
And why is it that you feel that way?

14:14.320 --> 14:18.080
Because that's how Will uses his magic.

14:18.080 --> 14:21.090
It's why I like him so much.

14:21.090 --> 14:26.470
Though I'm not crazy about the way he 
tends to put off his own happiness.

14:26.470 --> 14:28.150
B-Bee...

14:28.460 --> 14:30.850
I see, I see.

14:31.940 --> 14:33.650
Splendid.

14:50.840 --> 14:53.300
Allow me to properly introduce myself.

14:53.300 --> 14:56.490
I am a professor of the Academy 
and the Master of the Woods.

14:56.490 --> 14:59.000
My name is Hiram.

14:59.000 --> 15:02.270
I also serve as groundskeeper.

15:02.570 --> 15:04.080
Groundskeeper?

15:04.410 --> 15:07.240
It will be a bit of a special exception,

15:07.240 --> 15:11.220
but I will assume the responsibility of 
allowing you to tour the Academy.

15:11.220 --> 15:13.420
Now, young lady...

15:13.420 --> 15:17.610
What part of the Academy 
did you wish to see?

15:17.610 --> 15:19.400
W-Well...

15:22.130 --> 15:22.930
Um...

15:24.580 --> 15:26.560
I see, I see.

15:27.590 --> 15:30.200
In that case, let us go.

15:36.420 --> 15:38.590
What, what?! What is that?!

15:38.590 --> 15:40.590
There's a doll out there cleaning!

15:40.950 --> 15:45.240
That is a golem created by 
a previous Master of Forms.

15:45.240 --> 15:47.010
It's quite a handy thing to have.

15:47.830 --> 15:50.850
<i>Incredible... Its movements are so delicate.</i>

15:51.500 --> 15:54.670
<i>Even if the mana here is very stable,</i>

15:54.670 --> 15:57.360
<i>I can't imagine the work 
that must've gone into it.</i>

16:05.440 --> 16:06.610
By the way...

16:06.610 --> 16:11.100
How do you determine whether 
someone has a talent for magic?

16:11.100 --> 16:15.010
The words of those with talent have power.

16:15.010 --> 16:21.620
Both our Words of Creation and the everyday 
words we use have the same roots.

16:21.620 --> 16:26.620
The words of a child with talent 
just naturally make things happen.

16:26.620 --> 16:28.590
I know about that!

16:28.590 --> 16:31.570
When a kid like that really puts 
their all into cheering for you,

16:31.570 --> 16:33.580
you'll feel an inexplicable rush,

16:33.580 --> 16:36.090
or if someone who hates you 
says mean things to you,

16:36.090 --> 16:37.760
you can actually get hurt.

16:39.310 --> 16:40.480
Yes.

16:41.300 --> 16:44.110
It's said that the ones 
who make ideal sorcerers

16:44.110 --> 16:47.710
are often docile, easygoing, 
patient, and quiet.

16:47.710 --> 16:52.380
Those who are fierce by nature cannot 
help but use intense language.

16:52.380 --> 16:55.080
And if one continually 
uses intense language,

16:55.080 --> 16:58.800
they will eventually bring 
about their own ruin.

16:58.800 --> 17:03.910
<i>Gus used to tell me stories like 
that as warnings when I was little.</i>

17:03.910 --> 17:08.270
<i>It's a shared teaching that's omnipresent 
among those who use magic,</i>

17:09.030 --> 17:12.790
<i>and it's a teaching that's alive 
and well here at the Academy.</i>

17:15.350 --> 17:18.290
Well, here we are.

17:21.480 --> 17:26.090
This is what you wished to see: 
the Academy's library.

17:32.080 --> 17:34.360
I will personally authorize you

17:34.360 --> 17:38.820
to browse anywhere you like, 
excluding the forbidden shelves downstairs.

17:38.820 --> 17:41.640
I know my request was unreasonable.

17:41.640 --> 17:43.200
Thank you very much for granting it.

17:44.690 --> 17:48.040
Well, I shall be out in the courtyard.

17:48.040 --> 17:51.350
Should you need anything, just call me.

17:53.190 --> 17:55.780
So it was the books you wanted to see?

17:55.780 --> 17:57.740
Yep. Surprised?

17:57.740 --> 17:58.870
A bit.

17:58.870 --> 18:01.000
I thought you wanted to see 
where the sorcerers learned

18:01.000 --> 18:03.730
so you could use it as a 
reference for your songs.

18:04.010 --> 18:05.840
There's a book I'm hoping to find.

18:06.330 --> 18:07.530
Want some help?

18:09.490 --> 18:12.090
I'll search on my own for now.

18:12.090 --> 18:15.140
I might've made you bring me 
here only to end up boring you.

18:15.140 --> 18:16.360
Sorry.

18:20.480 --> 18:22.990
<i>An introduction to the history of magic...</i>

18:22.990 --> 18:25.440
<i>I learned a fair amount from Gus,</i>

18:25.440 --> 18:29.440
<i>but I wonder how much changed in 
the 200 years he wasn't aware of.</i>

18:35.590 --> 18:36.470
Bee.

18:37.380 --> 18:38.370
I'll hold those.

18:38.370 --> 18:40.060
Thanks.

18:44.800 --> 18:47.940
A record of Academy graduates...

18:47.940 --> 18:51.660
and a collection of local historical records?

19:28.140 --> 19:29.430
Hey, Bee...

19:29.760 --> 19:32.450
Wondering why was I looking 
for books like those?

19:36.440 --> 19:40.350
Long ago, before I became a troubadour,

19:40.350 --> 19:42.570
there was someone I traveled with.

19:42.570 --> 19:47.850
A lady with dull gold hair and eyes 
the same beautiful blue as the sea.

19:47.850 --> 19:51.480
We ended up together by chance, 
but we got on pretty well.

19:51.480 --> 19:55.080
I learned later that she 
was an amazing sorcerer.

19:55.580 --> 19:57.660
Apparently, she was traveling all around

19:57.660 --> 20:00.830
searching all kinds of ruins for 
Signs that have long been lost,

20:01.210 --> 20:04.870
but she was such a nice person that she 
took on a lot of people's problems.

20:04.870 --> 20:07.490
She wasn't that famous or anything,

20:07.490 --> 20:10.200
but in certain areas, 
she was known as a hero.

20:10.830 --> 20:14.260
I was having fun, too, so I made all 
kinds of detours to stay with her.

20:14.700 --> 20:17.390
Then, when it was time 
to go our separate ways,

20:17.390 --> 20:20.210
we waved at each other and 
said, "See you later."

20:21.530 --> 20:25.130
She died not long after we parted ways.

20:25.630 --> 20:30.510
I heard she died fighting a bunch 
of spectres to protect a town.

20:35.820 --> 20:37.330
That's so...

20:37.330 --> 20:39.510
Oh, don't get the wrong idea.

20:39.510 --> 20:42.340
It's not that I'm upset because she died.

20:42.340 --> 20:45.880
I mean, yeah, I'm sad, 
but she'd made up her mind, right?

20:46.220 --> 20:50.650
I'm not into criticizing things that 
someone's made up their mind about.

20:51.480 --> 20:54.650
But... still...

20:54.650 --> 20:58.660
I can't just sit around and let that kind 
of resolve be immediately forgotten.

20:59.020 --> 21:02.600
She was a hero, so her 
death was mourned by many.

21:02.600 --> 21:06.550
But even that was washed away by 
the passage of time and forgotten,

21:06.550 --> 21:09.790
until nobody even spoke her name anymore.

21:09.790 --> 21:12.430
This world is filled with dangers.

21:12.430 --> 21:15.570
Every time a hero is born, 
they're quickly forgotten.

21:15.570 --> 21:19.430
I guess that's just how it 
works, but... but still...

21:19.750 --> 21:22.970
They lauded her and thanked her, 
but when she died, that was the end of it.

21:22.970 --> 21:24.680
I can't stand that.

21:24.680 --> 21:27.930
A person's determination isn't 
something to use up and throw away!

21:28.680 --> 21:32.030
So I've been singing about her 
to keep her story alive.

21:32.460 --> 21:34.400
And along the way, I realized...

21:34.400 --> 21:35.430
Realized what?

21:35.710 --> 21:38.680
Songs of heroes hold hope!

21:39.030 --> 21:40.210
Hope?

21:40.210 --> 21:44.290
There's someone out there trying to save 
people with exceptional strength or magic.

21:44.290 --> 21:47.690
There's someone who's fighting, 
who's always been fighting, perhaps.

21:47.690 --> 21:51.940
And that brings a lot of hope to people!

21:51.940 --> 21:55.220
Just like the Three Heroes 
you're so fond of...

21:55.220 --> 21:57.570
and maybe even just like who you are now!

21:59.470 --> 22:00.720
Look!

22:02.120 --> 22:06.340
The first star that shines before 
the darkness of night sets in.

22:06.670 --> 22:08.660
That's what a hero is!

22:08.660 --> 22:12.240
When you walk, there are 
people who follow after you.

22:15.860 --> 22:17.970
Don't you think that's a great thing?

22:17.970 --> 22:19.380
Yeah, I do.

22:19.380 --> 22:21.580
And that's why I sing.

22:22.110 --> 22:25.210
To tell people there's a 
shining star right here!

22:27.980 --> 22:31.750
Okay, we're all done talking about me.

22:31.750 --> 22:35.490
Whew, after all that talking, 
I kind of want to sing now.

22:35.830 --> 22:36.990
Want to go sing somewhere?

22:37.410 --> 22:40.130
Yeah, yeah! Ready to make some money?

22:40.440 --> 22:41.360
Let's go.

22:41.360 --> 22:42.870
Well, then, since you'll be there,

22:42.870 --> 22:45.510
you can keep the crowd going 
and collect offerings!

22:45.510 --> 22:46.670
Right, got it.

22:47.500 --> 22:51.960
<i>I don't think Bee will ever 
settle down where I am.</i>

22:52.320 --> 22:54.850
Imagine, a paladin picking up coins for me!

22:54.850 --> 22:56.350
Talk about luxury!

22:56.800 --> 23:00.350
<i>Her conviction, as one who 
seeks and spreads songs,</i>

23:00.780 --> 23:04.860
<i>won't ever allow her to stay 
in one place for long.</i>

23:04.860 --> 23:09.960
<i>But even if she leaves, I know 
she'll come back eventually.</i>

23:09.960 --> 23:13.530
Hey, sing me the song about 
that sorcerer when it's done.

23:13.530 --> 23:16.740
Hmm...
Okay, I'll let you hear it.

23:16.740 --> 23:19.490
I've stocked up on plenty 
of information on her now!

23:21.140 --> 23:22.010
<i>One day,</i>

23:22.990 --> 23:25.900
<i>even if I meet my end in battle somewhere,</i>

23:26.500 --> 23:27.510
<i>I'm sure...</i>

23:28.510 --> 23:33.010
The Paladin and the Troubadour

23:35.180 --> 23:40.010
The Mad Forest
